{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > evidence/research.md <<'EOF'\n# Research provenance\n\n- Read the original Astrocade manual transcription: https://ballyalley.com/cart_manuals/text_manuals/incredible_wizard.txt . Cross-checked the scanned gameplay page in \"'`research/manual-page3.png` from https://ballyalley.com/cart_manuals/pdf_manuals/Incredible_Wizard,_The.pdf .\n- Read the December 1982 Videogaming Illustrated feature: https://vgpavilion.com/mags/1982/12/vi/conquering-the-incredible-wizard/ . It disagrees with the manual about some multiplier/life rules and reports Hard monster fire. The manual governs the interpretation. This game'\"'s hunters deliberately use contact attacks.\n- Downloaded the archived hardware recording through https://archive.org/metadata/IncredibleWizardBallyArcadeAstrocade1982 and inspected a frame at 65 seconds (\"'`research/hardware-frame.png`). Observed dark background, bright short creature silhouettes, cardinal lanes, visible paired gates and a compact radar without walls. Video/audio streams are Theora/Vorbis, about 331 seconds. No human listened; exact instrument synthesis and historical AI remain unknown.\n- Engine full handoff 0.89.1, git 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691. Read README, full API card, full asset specification, frame/camera/player guide sections, relevant index entries, ARCADE kit shell and maze. Native kit patterns are adapted into original scenes and simultaneous simulation.\n- Hub client 1.4.0, protocol 1, repo 35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869. Read README, client lifecycle and harness. Client bytes preserved by build.\n- All game-specific assets, maps, writing, animations, compositions and synthesized effects are new code. Native Humanoid, Blob, textured floor/walls and core candle are engine-provided. No source sprites, samples, music or maps reused.\nEOF\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'\"'EOF'\n\n## Milestone update — first complete simulation\n+- Full native engine and official unmodified Hub client pinned; prototype build is self-contained (~1.36 MB), no runtime fetches.\n+- Implemented content, deterministic simulation, input/storage/network adapters, coded audio, native art, native shell title/help/settings/credits/results/dev, attract showcase.\n+- A non-cheating Normal command pilot (seed 1972) cleared all 6 rooms, 136 hunters, 6 familiar catches, 5 one-hit Wizard manifestations in 586.25 simulated seconds, losing 1 life. Bell rang once; portal coverage still to add to campaign driver.\n+- Packaged Chromium boots from file:// and normal play has no runtime errors. First title/gameplay screenshots inspected. Title typography/menu overflows vertically and needs correction; board/radar readable.\n+- Fixed a critical build bug found by packaged browser: String.replace treated engine dollar sequences as replacement syntax, corrupting inline JS. Build now uses callbacks. Native map legend warnings also fixed.\n+- Next: comprehensive invariant/alternate-outcome tests, Hub harness, input/touch/dev/audio checks, visual polish, final metadata.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > evidence/research.md <<'EOF'\n# Research provenance\n\n- Read the original Astrocade manual transcription: https://ballyalley.com/cart_manuals/text_manuals/incredible_wizard.txt . Cross-checked the scanned gameplay page in \"'`research/manual-page3.png` from https://ballyalley.com/cart_manuals/pdf_manuals/Incredible_Wizard,_The.pdf .\n- Read the December 1982 Videogaming Illustrated feature: https://vgpavilion.com/mags/1982/12/vi/conquering-the-incredible-wizard/ . It disagrees with the manual about some multiplier/life rules and reports Hard monster fire. The manual governs the interpretation. This game'\"'s hunters deliberately use contact attacks.\n- Downloaded the archived hardware recording through https://archive.org/metadata/IncredibleWizardBallyArcadeAstrocade1982 and inspected a frame at 65 seconds (\"'`research/hardware-frame.png`). Observed dark background, bright short creature silhouettes, cardinal lanes, visible paired gates and a compact radar without walls. Video/audio streams are Theora/Vorbis, about 331 seconds. No human listened; exact instrument synthesis and historical AI remain unknown.\n- Engine full handoff 0.89.1, git 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691. Read README, full API card, full asset specification, frame/camera/player guide sections, relevant index entries, ARCADE kit shell and maze. Native kit patterns are adapted into original scenes and simultaneous simulation.\n- Hub client 1.4.0, protocol 1, repo 35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869. Read README, client lifecycle and harness. Client bytes preserved by build.\n- All game-specific assets, maps, writing, animations, compositions and synthesized effects are new code. Native Humanoid, Blob, textured floor/walls and core candle are engine-provided. No source sprites, samples, music or maps reused.\nEOF\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'\"'EOF'\n\n## Milestone update — first complete simulation\n+- Full native engine and official unmodified Hub client pinned; prototype build is self-contained (~1.36 MB), no runtime fetches.\n+- Implemented content, deterministic simulation, input/storage/network adapters, coded audio, native art, native shell title/help/settings/credits/results/dev, attract showcase.\n+- A non-cheating Normal command pilot (seed 1972) cleared all 6 rooms, 136 hunters, 6 familiar catches, 5 one-hit Wizard manifestations in 586.25 simulated seconds, losing 1 life. Bell rang once; portal coverage still to add to campaign driver.\n+- Packaged Chromium boots from file:// and normal play has no runtime errors. First title/gameplay screenshots inspected. Title typography/menu overflows vertically and needs correction; board/radar readable.\n+- Fixed a critical build bug found by packaged browser: String.replace treated engine dollar sequences as replacement syntax, corrupting inline JS. Build now uses callbacks. Native map legend warnings also fixed.\n+- Next: comprehensive invariant/alternate-outcome tests, Hub harness, input/touch/dev/audio checks, visual polish, final metadata.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='index.template.html';s=open(p).read().replace('</style>', '.esh .esh-ttl{display:flex\"'!important;align-items:center!important;padding:20px 5%!important}.esh .esh-ttl>div{width:47%!important;max-width:440px!important;padding:0!important}.esh .esh-ttl h1{font-size:2.5em!important;line-height:.97!important;margin-bottom:12px!important}.esh .esh-ttl .esh-k{font-size:.64em;letter-spacing:.20em;white-space:nowrap}.esh .esh-ttl .esh-sub{font-size:.9em!important;max-width:none}.esh .esh-ttl .esh-btns{margin-top:20px!important;max-width:250px!important;gap:7px!important}.esh .esh-ttl button{padding:8px 16px!important;min-height:39px!important}.esh .esh-ttl .esh-tags{font-size:10px!important;letter-spacing:.04em}.esh .esh-ttl .esh-m{font-size:11px}@media(max-aspect-ratio:1/1){.esh .esh-ttl>div{width:100%!important}.esh .esh-ttl h1{font-size:2.5em!important}.esh .esh-ttl .esh-k{white-space:normal}.esh .esh-ttl .esh-btns{max-width:100%!important}}'\"\\\\n</style>');open(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/main.js';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"text:'The sorcerer has a condition.\\\\\\\\nYou have a lantern-rifle.',\\\",'').replace(\\\"app.audio.update(null,dt);},draw\\\", \\\"app.stage.titleWizard.update(dt,{x:220,y:110,pose:'cast',facing:Math.PI/2,expr:'angry'});app.audio.update(null,dt);},draw\\\");open(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/art.js';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"this.titleWizard.update(1/120,{x,y,pose:'cast',facing:Math.PI/2,expr:'angry'});\\\",'');open(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/audio.js';s=open(p).read();start=s.index(' voice(seed){');end=s.index('\\\\n stop(){',start)\ns=s[:start]+''' voice(seed){const a=this.game.audio,c=a.ctx,bus=a.bus('voice');if(\"'!c||!bus||this.stopped)return;for(let i=0;i<6;i++){const n=(seed*31+i*17)%7,o=c.createOscillator(),f=c.createBiquadFilter(),g=c.createGain(),t=c.currentTime+i*.075,d=.06+n*.005;o.type=i%2?'\"'triangle':'sawtooth';o.frequency.setValueAtTime(150+n*33,t);o.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(210+n*25,t+d);f.type='bandpass';f.frequency.setValueAtTime(700+n*220,t);f.Q.value=2;g.gain.setValueAtTime(0,t);g.gain.linearRampToValueAtTime(.10,t+.008);g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(.0001,t+d);o.connect(f);f.connect(g);g.connect(bus);o.start(t);o.stop(t+d+.015);o.onended=()=>{o.disconnect();f.disconnect();g.disconnect();};this.voiceHandles.push(o);}this.voiceHandles=this.voiceHandles.slice(-36);}\n''' +s[end:]\ns=s.replace(\\\"for(const h of this.voiceHandles)h.stop?.();\\\", \\\"for(const h of this.voiceHandles){try{h.stop?.();}catch{}}\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nnode tools/build.mjs\n/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python tests/first-look.py > evidence/first-look-state.txt\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
