{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_81","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# The Incurable Wizard\n\nOne bolt. Six floors. No known cure.\n\nOpen the HTML beside this folder from \"'`file://` to play. There are no runtime downloads or audio files. AI Hub supplies online sessions; standalone co-op shares one screen.\n\n## Build and verify\n\n- `npm run build` writes the byte-identical development/test and root release HTML, and the root exit interview.\n- `npm test` runs simulation, full ordinary-command campaigns, packaging, Chromium/Firefox/WebKit input/audio checks, and Hub lifecycle/shared-combat checks. Normal output is failures followed by one count line. The browser runner starts its own localhost server on an OS-selected port and stops it afterward.\n- `node tools/verify.mjs --core` runs only deterministic simulation and protocol edge checks after a simulation change.\n\nInstalled Python Playwright 1.63.0 is used at `/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python`. No installation is necessary on the supplied workstation. No frame-rate gate is imposed.\n\n## Controls\n\nLeft stick / WASD move. Right stick / arrow keys / mouse aim. R2 / Cross / Space / click commit the sole bolt. Options / Escape pause. Touch has two invisible anchored thumb areas and optional visible-target auto-fire. Native Settings includes sound, comfort, glyphs, controls and rebinding.\n\nCouch setup explicitly assigns keyboard + pad, two pads, or a shared keyboard. Shared-keyboard P2 uses IJKL, numpad 8/4/2/6, and right Shift. Online is launched by AI Hub; a title button cannot provide Internet matchmaking because the supplied Hub protocol has no standalone matchmaking API.\n\n## Architecture\n\n`src/content.js` is the designer data and balance defaults. `src/sim.js` owns fixed-step rules, seeded AI, scoring, visibility, checkpoints and serializable state. `platform.js` owns device adapters, versioned storage and the authoritative Hub wire protocol. `art.js` uses the full native render queue, Humanoid/Blob rigs and original shapes/weapon; `audio.js` contains every sound and composition. `main.js` wires the native TV shell, scenes, results, help, credits, developer pages and private attract simulation.\n\nEngine: full my-3D2dge 0.89.1, commit 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691. Hub: unmodified client 1.4.0, protocol 1, commit 35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869. Engine source is unmodified. Adapters extend native APIs for simultaneous rules, invisible touch sticks and live online overlays. The official Hub script is embedded first after charset, byte for byte.\n\nThe logical landscape base is 640×360, expanded to the screen. Portrait uses the engine'\"'s 400×640 portrait override. A fixed arena camera fits every route; wheel and pinch zoom are disabled. One tile is always 16 world units. Simulation updates at 120 Hz independently of rendering.\n\n## Evidence\n\n\"'`evidence/verification.json`, `browser-results.json`, `hub-harness.json`, `shared-combat.json` and `audio.json` contain checks and measurements. Research provenance is in `evidence/research.md`. Targeted PNGs cover title, bells, finale, developer panels, credits and touch framing. Hardware/physical-device listening and human first-run pacing are not available; automated pilots are separate evidence.\nEOF\ncat > content/AUTHORING.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Authoring another chamber\n\nEdit only the declarative descriptions/layouts/spawn data in \"'`src/content.js` for ordinary content changes.\n\nThe board is 21×13 cells. `#` is stone, `.` is walkable floor, `B` is a solid shootable bell, and the two `P` mouths are at (0,6)/(20,6). Leave a reachable path between both entrances, the familiar'\"'s (10,1) start, all bell-adjacent cells, the center waypoint (10,6) and both gates. The verifier tests every walkable cell and scheduled spawn against the same authoritative Grid.\n\nEach spawn has a family, earliest active Hunt time, minimum kill count (\"'`after`), and legal warning cell. Budgets are finite. The final three obligations in each room are stronger replacements unlocked after specified kills. The director needs every obligation exhausted, including delayed warnings, before releasing the familiar. Spawn warnings grant about 0.9 seconds before contact becomes dangerous.\n\n`intrusions` is 0, 1, or 3. Ordinary authored intrusions may leave after four missed windows. The final three manifestations are separate one-hit entities; they change firing rhythm, not hit points. The last floor'\"'s declared 5,000 bounty consumes its earned next multiplier only once.\n\nA native tile is 16 world units. GridMover positions are cell coordinates; \"'`IW.world(cell)` adds the half-cell center and scales by 16. Never store screen coordinates in gameplay. Cosmetic random state must not consume World.rand(). Bell lure uses legal path distance; visibility uses an unobstructed cardinal lane from either living player.\n\nRun `node tools/verify.mjs --core` after content/balance changes. Rebuild and run `npm test` for integration or release. Native pause → Developer provides live sliders and room/encounter tools; changes mark Practice. Reset restores the clock, invulnerability and all balance overrides. Hub rounds expose only local diagnostics.\nEOF\ncat > evidence/issues.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Distinct implementation issues found and fixed\n\nAssertions repaired because the test itself was wrong are not counted as game defects.\n\n1. **Critical:** build-time String.replace expanded dollar sequences inside the engine. The packaged engine failed to parse. Callback replacements now preserve script bytes/semantics.\n2. Native map warnings for unregistered bell/gate characters. Added explicit legend tags.\n3. Title typography and actions overflowed the 1080p frame. Corrected the native shell title sizing and padding.\n4. **Critical:** two authored central walls occupied the familiar waypoint/spawn cell, which could trap an uncaught familiar. Validated and opened those cells; all rooms and spawn coordinates are now connected.\n5. Bell reveal/lure timers stopped expiring outside Hunt. Moved their clocks into the phase-independent fixed step.\n6. Developer modal height used viewport units inside the TV-scaled shell and could place Resume outside the viewport. Bounded it relative to its native shell and enabled internal scrolling.\n7. Reassigning a previously active controller to a different couch seat could produce a false disconnect pause. Explicit device reassignment now resets the primary input's previous pad identity.\n8. High-density portrait screens expanded the logical buffer too far, making the game and HUD unnecessarily small. Added the engine's portrait resolution override and verified both orientations.\n9. Terminal network state could finish between periodic snapshots. Terminal snapshots now repeat and the host waits for peer acknowledgement before reporting a completed campaign, with a bounded fallback; time-up still reports immediately within grace.\n\nHeadless pilot route mistakes, a test firing toward the outer wall, a TileMap.center array/object assumption, pre-draw screenshot state, and expected iframe count after host removal were test defects, not additional game issues.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_81","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# The Incurable Wizard\n\nOne bolt. Six floors. No known cure.\n\nOpen the HTML beside this folder from \"'`file://` to play. There are no runtime downloads or audio files. AI Hub supplies online sessions; standalone co-op shares one screen.\n\n## Build and verify\n\n- `npm run build` writes the byte-identical development/test and root release HTML, and the root exit interview.\n- `npm test` runs simulation, full ordinary-command campaigns, packaging, Chromium/Firefox/WebKit input/audio checks, and Hub lifecycle/shared-combat checks. Normal output is failures followed by one count line. The browser runner starts its own localhost server on an OS-selected port and stops it afterward.\n- `node tools/verify.mjs --core` runs only deterministic simulation and protocol edge checks after a simulation change.\n\nInstalled Python Playwright 1.63.0 is used at `/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python`. No installation is necessary on the supplied workstation. No frame-rate gate is imposed.\n\n## Controls\n\nLeft stick / WASD move. Right stick / arrow keys / mouse aim. R2 / Cross / Space / click commit the sole bolt. Options / Escape pause. Touch has two invisible anchored thumb areas and optional visible-target auto-fire. Native Settings includes sound, comfort, glyphs, controls and rebinding.\n\nCouch setup explicitly assigns keyboard + pad, two pads, or a shared keyboard. Shared-keyboard P2 uses IJKL, numpad 8/4/2/6, and right Shift. Online is launched by AI Hub; a title button cannot provide Internet matchmaking because the supplied Hub protocol has no standalone matchmaking API.\n\n## Architecture\n\n`src/content.js` is the designer data and balance defaults. `src/sim.js` owns fixed-step rules, seeded AI, scoring, visibility, checkpoints and serializable state. `platform.js` owns device adapters, versioned storage and the authoritative Hub wire protocol. `art.js` uses the full native render queue, Humanoid/Blob rigs and original shapes/weapon; `audio.js` contains every sound and composition. `main.js` wires the native TV shell, scenes, results, help, credits, developer pages and private attract simulation.\n\nEngine: full my-3D2dge 0.89.1, commit 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691. Hub: unmodified client 1.4.0, protocol 1, commit 35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869. Engine source is unmodified. Adapters extend native APIs for simultaneous rules, invisible touch sticks and live online overlays. The official Hub script is embedded first after charset, byte for byte.\n\nThe logical landscape base is 640×360, expanded to the screen. Portrait uses the engine'\"'s 400×640 portrait override. A fixed arena camera fits every route; wheel and pinch zoom are disabled. One tile is always 16 world units. Simulation updates at 120 Hz independently of rendering.\n\n## Evidence\n\n\"'`evidence/verification.json`, `browser-results.json`, `hub-harness.json`, `shared-combat.json` and `audio.json` contain checks and measurements. Research provenance is in `evidence/research.md`. Targeted PNGs cover title, bells, finale, developer panels, credits and touch framing. Hardware/physical-device listening and human first-run pacing are not available; automated pilots are separate evidence.\nEOF\ncat > content/AUTHORING.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Authoring another chamber\n\nEdit only the declarative descriptions/layouts/spawn data in \"'`src/content.js` for ordinary content changes.\n\nThe board is 21×13 cells. `#` is stone, `.` is walkable floor, `B` is a solid shootable bell, and the two `P` mouths are at (0,6)/(20,6). Leave a reachable path between both entrances, the familiar'\"'s (10,1) start, all bell-adjacent cells, the center waypoint (10,6) and both gates. The verifier tests every walkable cell and scheduled spawn against the same authoritative Grid.\n\nEach spawn has a family, earliest active Hunt time, minimum kill count (\"'`after`), and legal warning cell. Budgets are finite. The final three obligations in each room are stronger replacements unlocked after specified kills. The director needs every obligation exhausted, including delayed warnings, before releasing the familiar. Spawn warnings grant about 0.9 seconds before contact becomes dangerous.\n\n`intrusions` is 0, 1, or 3. Ordinary authored intrusions may leave after four missed windows. The final three manifestations are separate one-hit entities; they change firing rhythm, not hit points. The last floor'\"'s declared 5,000 bounty consumes its earned next multiplier only once.\n\nA native tile is 16 world units. GridMover positions are cell coordinates; \"'`IW.world(cell)` adds the half-cell center and scales by 16. Never store screen coordinates in gameplay. Cosmetic random state must not consume World.rand(). Bell lure uses legal path distance; visibility uses an unobstructed cardinal lane from either living player.\n\nRun `node tools/verify.mjs --core` after content/balance changes. Rebuild and run `npm test` for integration or release. Native pause → Developer provides live sliders and room/encounter tools; changes mark Practice. Reset restores the clock, invulnerability and all balance overrides. Hub rounds expose only local diagnostics.\nEOF\ncat > evidence/issues.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Distinct implementation issues found and fixed\n\nAssertions repaired because the test itself was wrong are not counted as game defects.\n\n1. **Critical:** build-time String.replace expanded dollar sequences inside the engine. The packaged engine failed to parse. Callback replacements now preserve script bytes/semantics.\n2. Native map warnings for unregistered bell/gate characters. Added explicit legend tags.\n3. Title typography and actions overflowed the 1080p frame. Corrected the native shell title sizing and padding.\n4. **Critical:** two authored central walls occupied the familiar waypoint/spawn cell, which could trap an uncaught familiar. Validated and opened those cells; all rooms and spawn coordinates are now connected.\n5. Bell reveal/lure timers stopped expiring outside Hunt. Moved their clocks into the phase-independent fixed step.\n6. Developer modal height used viewport units inside the TV-scaled shell and could place Resume outside the viewport. Bounded it relative to its native shell and enabled internal scrolling.\n7. Reassigning a previously active controller to a different couch seat could produce a false disconnect pause. Explicit device reassignment now resets the primary input's previous pad identity.\n8. High-density portrait screens expanded the logical buffer too far, making the game and HUD unnecessarily small. Added the engine's portrait resolution override and verified both orientations.\n9. Terminal network state could finish between periodic snapshots. Terminal snapshots now repeat and the host waits for peer acknowledgement before reporting a completed campaign, with a bounded fallback; time-up still reports immediately within grace.\n\nHeadless pilot route mistakes, a test firing toward the outer wall, a TileMap.center array/object assumption, pre-draw screenshot state, and expected iframe count after host removal were test defects, not additional game issues.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
